      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the tip. i'm actually on warfarin right now for a blood thinner thing, so i've been told by my doctor to be careful with what i eat, but i feel like i can handle more nutrition if i do it right. if i just try to keep it consistent, like maybe a big smoothie with a bunch of kale and spinach every morning, would that be fine for my heart? i just want to make sure i'm doing the most i can.",
